<p align=3D"center"> <em><strong>An algorithm for CRT</strong></em> </p>
<div class=3D"wordads-ad-wrapper" style=3D"display: inherit;"><div id=3D"at=
atags-26942-325057"></div></div><p>Now we describe the algorithm that is de=
scribed by the above two examples. Suppose that the following system of equ=
ations such that the moduli <img src=3D"https://s0.wp.com/latex.php?latex=
=3Dm1%2Cm_2%2C%5Ccdots%2Cm_t&amp;bg=3Dffffff&amp;fg=3D333333&amp;s=3D0&amp;=
c=3D20201002" alt=3D"m1,m_2,\cdots,m_t" class=3D"latex"> are pairwise relat=
ively prime and such that each equation by itself has a unique solution, i.=
e. <img src=3D"https://s0.wp.com/latex.php?latex=3Da_i&amp;bg=3Dffffff&amp;=
fg=3D333333&amp;s=3D0&amp;c=3D20201002" alt=3D"a_i" class=3D"latex"> and <i=
mg src=3D"https://s0.wp.com/latex.php?latex=3Dm_i&amp;bg=3Dffffff&amp;fg=3D=
333333&amp;s=3D0&amp;c=3D20201002" alt=3D"m_i" class=3D"latex"> are relativ=
ely prime for each <img src=3D"https://s0.wp.com/latex.php?latex=3Di&amp;bg=
=3Dffffff&amp;fg=3D333333&amp;s=3D0&amp;c=3D20201002" alt=3D"i" class=3D"la=
tex">.</p>
<ul>
<img src=3D"https://s0.wp.com/latex.php?latex=3Da_1+%5C+x+%5Cequiv+b_1+%5C+=
%28%5Ctext%7Bmod%7D+%5C+m_1%29&amp;bg=3Dffffff&amp;fg=3D333333&amp;s=3D0&am=
p;c=3D20201002" alt=3D"a_1 \ x \equiv b_1 \ (\text{mod} \ m_1)" class=3D"la=
tex"><p></p>
<p><img src=3D"https://s0.wp.com/latex.php?latex=3Da_2+%5C+x+%5Cequiv+b_2+%=
5C+%28%5Ctext%7Bmod%7D+%5C+m_2%29&amp;bg=3Dffffff&amp;fg=3D333333&amp;s=3D0=
&amp;c=3D20201002" alt=3D"a_2 \ x \equiv b_2 \ (\text{mod} \ m_2)" class=3D=
"latex"></p>
<ul>
<img src=3D"https://s0.wp.com/latex.php?latex=3D%5Ccdots&amp;bg=3Dffffff&am=
p;fg=3D333333&amp;s=3D0&amp;c=3D20201002" alt=3D"\cdots" class=3D"latex"><p=
></p>
</ul>
<p><img src=3D"https://s0.wp.com/latex.php?latex=3Da_%7Bt-1%7D+%5C++x+%5Ceq=
uiv+b_%7Bt-1%7D+%5C+%28%5Ctext%7Bmod%7D+%5C+m_%7Bt-1%7D%29&amp;bg=3Dffffff&=
amp;fg=3D333333&amp;s=3D0&amp;c=3D20201002" alt=3D"a_{t-1} \  x \equiv b_{t=
-1} \ (\text{mod} \ m_{t-1})" class=3D"latex"></p>
<p><img src=3D"https://s0.wp.com/latex.php?latex=3Da_t+%5C++x+%5Cequiv+b_t+=
%5C+%28%5Ctext%7Bmod%7D+%5C+m_t%29&amp;bg=3Dffffff&amp;fg=3D333333&amp;s=3D=
0&amp;c=3D20201002" alt=3D"a_t \  x \equiv b_t \ (\text{mod} \ m_t)" class=
=3D"latex"></p>
</ul>
<p>The following three steps describe how to obtain the solution to this sy=
stem of equations.</p>
<p><strong><em>Step 1</em></strong><br>
Solve each equation <img src=3D"https://s0.wp.com/latex.php?latex=3Da_i+%5C=
+x+%5Cequiv+b_i+%5C+%28%5Ctext%7Bmod%7D+%5C+m_i%29&amp;bg=3Dffffff&amp;fg=
=3D333333&amp;s=3D0&amp;c=3D20201002" alt=3D"a_i \ x \equiv b_i \ (\text{mo=
d} \ m_i)" class=3D"latex"> individually to obtain the solution <img src=3D=
"https://s0.wp.com/latex.php?latex=3Dx+%5Cequiv+c_i+%5C+%28%5Ctext%7Bmod%7D=
+%5C+m_i%29&amp;bg=3Dffffff&amp;fg=3D333333&amp;s=3D0&amp;c=3D20201002" alt=
=3D"x \equiv c_i \ (\text{mod} \ m_i)" class=3D"latex">. The original syste=
m is equivalent to the following equivalent system of equations, i.e. any s=
olution to one system is the solution to the other.</p>
<ul>
<img src=3D"https://s0.wp.com/latex.php?latex=3Dx+%5Cequiv+c_1+%5C+%28%5Cte=
xt%7Bmod%7D+%5C+m_1%29&amp;bg=3Dffffff&amp;fg=3D333333&amp;s=3D0&amp;c=3D20=
201002" alt=3D"x \equiv c_1 \ (\text{mod} \ m_1)" class=3D"latex"><p></p>
<p><img src=3D"https://s0.wp.com/latex.php?latex=3Dx+%5Cequiv+c_2+%5C+%28%5=
Ctext%7Bmod%7D+%5C+m_2%29&amp;bg=3Dffffff&amp;fg=3D333333&amp;s=3D0&amp;c=
=3D20201002" alt=3D"x \equiv c_2 \ (\text{mod} \ m_2)" class=3D"latex"></p>
<ul>
<img src=3D"https://s0.wp.com/latex.php?latex=3D%5Ccdots&amp;bg=3Dffffff&am=
p;fg=3D333333&amp;s=3D0&amp;c=3D20201002" alt=3D"\cdots" class=3D"latex"><p=
></p>
</ul>
<p><img src=3D"https://s0.wp.com/latex.php?latex=3Dx+%5Cequiv+c_%7Bt-1%7D+%=
5C+%28%5Ctext%7Bmod%7D+%5C+m_%7Bt-1%7D%29&amp;bg=3Dffffff&amp;fg=3D333333&a=
mp;s=3D0&amp;c=3D20201002" alt=3D"x \equiv c_{t-1} \ (\text{mod} \ m_{t-1})=
" class=3D"latex"></p>
<p><img src=3D"https://s0.wp.com/latex.php?latex=3Dx+%5Cequiv+c_t+%5C+%28%5=
Ctext%7Bmod%7D+%5C+m_t%29&amp;bg=3Dffffff&amp;fg=3D333333&amp;s=3D0&amp;c=
=3D20201002" alt=3D"x \equiv c_t \ (\text{mod} \ m_t)" class=3D"latex"></p>
</ul>
<p><strong><em>Step 2</em></strong><br>
For each <img src=3D"https://s0.wp.com/latex.php?latex=3Di&amp;bg=3Dffffff&=
amp;fg=3D333333&amp;s=3D0&amp;c=3D20201002" alt=3D"i" class=3D"latex">, let=
 <img src=3D"https://s0.wp.com/latex.php?latex=3Dn_i&amp;bg=3Dffffff&amp;fg=
=3D333333&amp;s=3D0&amp;c=3D20201002" alt=3D"n_i" class=3D"latex"> be the p=
roduct of all moduli <img src=3D"https://s0.wp.com/latex.php?latex=3Dm_j&am=
p;bg=3Dffffff&amp;fg=3D333333&amp;s=3D0&amp;c=3D20201002" alt=3D"m_j" class=
=3D"latex"> where <img src=3D"https://s0.wp.com/latex.php?latex=3Dj+%5Cne+i=
&amp;bg=3Dffffff&amp;fg=3D333333&amp;s=3D0&amp;c=3D20201002" alt=3D"j \ne i=
" class=3D"latex">. Each <img src=3D"https://s0.wp.com/latex.php?latex=3Dn_=
i&amp;bg=3Dffffff&amp;fg=3D333333&amp;s=3D0&amp;c=3D20201002" alt=3D"n_i" c=
lass=3D"latex"> is relatively prime to <img src=3D"https://s0.wp.com/latex.=
php?latex=3Dm_i&amp;bg=3Dffffff&amp;fg=3D333333&amp;s=3D0&amp;c=3D20201002"=
 alt=3D"m_i" class=3D"latex">. Thus <img src=3D"https://s0.wp.com/latex.php=
?latex=3Dn_i&amp;bg=3Dffffff&amp;fg=3D333333&amp;s=3D0&amp;c=3D20201002" al=
t=3D"n_i" class=3D"latex"> has a multiplicative inverse modulo <img src=3D"=
https://s0.wp.com/latex.php?latex=3Dm_i&amp;bg=3Dffffff&amp;fg=3D333333&amp=
;s=3D0&amp;c=3D20201002" alt=3D"m_i" class=3D"latex">. Equivalently solve t=
he following equations individually.</p>
<ul>
<img src=3D"https://s0.wp.com/latex.php?latex=3Dn_1+%5C+y+%5Cequiv+1+%5C+%2=
8%5Ctext%7Bmod%7D+%5C+m_1%29&amp;bg=3Dffffff&amp;fg=3D333333&amp;s=3D0&amp;=
c=3D20201002" alt=3D"n_1 \ y \equiv 1 \ (\text{mod} \ m_1)" class=3D"latex"=
><p></p>
<p><img src=3D"https://s0.wp.com/latex.php?latex=3Dn_2+%5C+y+%5Cequiv+1+%5C=
+%28%5Ctext%7Bmod%7D+%5C+m_2%29&amp;bg=3Dffffff&amp;fg=3D333333&amp;s=3D0&a=
mp;c=3D20201002" alt=3D"n_2 \ y \equiv 1 \ (\text{mod} \ m_2)" class=3D"lat=
ex"></p>
<ul>
<img src=3D"https://s0.wp.com/latex.php?latex=3D%5Ccdots&amp;bg=3Dffffff&am=
p;fg=3D333333&amp;s=3D0&amp;c=3D20201002" alt=3D"\cdots" class=3D"latex"><p=
></p>
</ul>
<p><img src=3D"https://s0.wp.com/latex.php?latex=3Dn_%7Bt-1%7D+%5C++y+%5Ceq=
uiv+1+%5C+%28%5Ctext%7Bmod%7D+%5C+m_%7Bt-1%7D%29&amp;bg=3Dffffff&amp;fg=3D3=
33333&amp;s=3D0&amp;c=3D20201002" alt=3D"n_{t-1} \  y \equiv 1 \ (\text{mod=
} \ m_{t-1})" class=3D"latex"></p>
<p><img src=3D"https://s0.wp.com/latex.php?latex=3Dn_t+%5C++y+%5Cequiv+1+%5=
C+%28%5Ctext%7Bmod%7D+%5C+m_t%29&amp;bg=3Dffffff&amp;fg=3D333333&amp;s=3D0&=
amp;c=3D20201002" alt=3D"n_t \  y \equiv 1 \ (\text{mod} \ m_t)" class=3D"l=
atex"></p>
</ul>
<p>For each <img src=3D"https://s0.wp.com/latex.php?latex=3Di&amp;bg=3Dffff=
ff&amp;fg=3D333333&amp;s=3D0&amp;c=3D20201002" alt=3D"i" class=3D"latex">, =
let <img src=3D"https://s0.wp.com/latex.php?latex=3Dw_i&amp;bg=3Dffffff&amp=
;fg=3D333333&amp;s=3D0&amp;c=3D20201002" alt=3D"w_i" class=3D"latex"> be th=
e inverse of <img src=3D"https://s0.wp.com/latex.php?latex=3Dn_i&amp;bg=3Df=
fffff&amp;fg=3D333333&amp;s=3D0&amp;c=3D20201002" alt=3D"n_i" class=3D"late=
x"> modulo <img src=3D"https://s0.wp.com/latex.php?latex=3Dm_i&amp;bg=3Dfff=
fff&amp;fg=3D333333&amp;s=3D0&amp;c=3D20201002" alt=3D"m_i" class=3D"latex"=
>, i.e. <img src=3D"https://s0.wp.com/latex.php?latex=3Dn_i%5E%7B-1%7D+%5Ce=
quiv+w_i+%5C+%28%5Ctext%7Bmod%7D+%5C+m_i%29&amp;bg=3Dffffff&amp;fg=3D333333=
&amp;s=3D0&amp;c=3D20201002" alt=3D"n_i^{-1} \equiv w_i \ (\text{mod} \ m_i=
)" class=3D"latex">.</p>
<div class=3D"wordads-ad-wrapper" style=3D"display: inherit;"><div id=3D"at=
atags-26942-728477"></div></div><p><strong><em>Step 3</em></strong><br>
The solution is given by </p>
<ul>
<img src=3D"https://s0.wp.com/latex.php?latex=3Dx_0+%5Cequiv+c_1+%5Ccdot+n_=
1+%5Ccdot+w_1%2Bc_2+%5Ccdot+n_2+%5Ccdot+w_2%2B%5Ccdots%2Bc_t+%5Ccdot+n_t+%5=
Ccdot+w_t+%5C+%28%5Ctext%7Bmod%7D+%5C+m%29&amp;bg=3Dffffff&amp;fg=3D333333&=
amp;s=3D0&amp;c=3D20201002" alt=3D"x_0 \equiv c_1 \cdot n_1 \cdot w_1+c_2 \=
cdot n_2 \cdot w_2+\cdots+c_t \cdot n_t \cdot w_t \ (\text{mod} \ m)" class=
=3D"latex">
</ul>
<p>where <img src=3D"https://s0.wp.com/latex.php?latex=3Dm%3Dm_1+%5Ccdot+m_=
2+%5Ccdots+m_t&amp;bg=3Dffffff&amp;fg=3D333333&amp;s=3D0&amp;c=3D20201002" =
alt=3D"m=3Dm_1 \cdot m_2 \cdots m_t" class=3D"latex">.</p>
<p>Let=E2=80=99s look at what the algorithm entails computationally. Step 1=
 requires solving a set of linear congruence equations individually (equiva=
lently, solving linear diophantine equations individually), unless the equa=
tions are given in the form <img src=3D"https://s0.wp.com/latex.php?latex=
=3Dx+%5Cequiv+c_i+%5C+%28%5Ctext%7Bmod%7D+%5C+m_i%29&amp;bg=3Dffffff&amp;fg=
=3D333333&amp;s=3D0&amp;c=3D20201002" alt=3D"x \equiv c_i \ (\text{mod} \ m=
_i)" class=3D"latex">. The extended Euclidean algorithm is an excellent app=
roach, especially in computer implementation.</p>
<p>Step 2 involves finding multiplicative inverses of the numbers <img src=
=3D"https://s0.wp.com/latex.php?latex=3Dn_i&amp;bg=3Dffffff&amp;fg=3D333333=
&amp;s=3D0&amp;c=3D20201002" alt=3D"n_i" class=3D"latex">. The extended Euc=
lidean algorithm is also an excellent approach, especially in computer impl=
ementation.</p>
<p>Step 3 is to gather up the results from Step 1 and Step 2. The computati=
on here is to reduce modulo <img src=3D"https://s0.wp.com/latex.php?latex=
=3Dm%3Dm_1+%5Ccdot+m_2+%5Ccdots+m_t&amp;bg=3Dffffff&amp;fg=3D333333&amp;s=
=3D0&amp;c=3D20201002" alt=3D"m=3Dm_1 \cdot m_2 \cdots m_t" class=3D"latex"=
>.</p>
<p>________________________________________________________________________=
____</p>
<p align=3D"center"> <em><strong>Why does the algorithm work?</strong></em>=
 </p>
<p>The number <img src=3D"https://s0.wp.com/latex.php?latex=3Dx_0+%5Cequiv+=
c_1+%5Ccdot+n_1+%5Ccdot+w_1%2Bc_2+%5Ccdot+n_2+%5Ccdot+w_2%2B%5Ccdots%2Bc_t+=
%5Ccdot+n_t+%5Ccdot+w_t+%5C+%28%5Ctext%7Bmod%7D+%5C+m%29&amp;bg=3Dffffff&am=
p;fg=3D333333&amp;s=3D0&amp;c=3D20201002" alt=3D"x_0 \equiv c_1 \cdot n_1 \=
cdot w_1+c_2 \cdot n_2 \cdot w_2+\cdots+c_t \cdot n_t \cdot w_t \ (\text{mo=
d} \ m)" class=3D"latex"> is a solution to each of the equations in the giv=
en system of linear congruence equations. To see that <img src=3D"https://s=
0.wp.com/latex.php?latex=3Dx_0&amp;bg=3Dffffff&amp;fg=3D333333&amp;s=3D0&am=
p;c=3D20201002" alt=3D"x_0" class=3D"latex"> is a solution to the equation =
<img src=3D"https://s0.wp.com/latex.php?latex=3Da_1+%5C+x+%5Cequiv+b_1+%5C+=
%28%5Ctext%7Bmod%7D+%5C+m_1%29&amp;bg=3Dffffff&amp;fg=3D333333&amp;s=3D0&am=
p;c=3D20201002" alt=3D"a_1 \ x \equiv b_1 \ (\text{mod} \ m_1)" class=3D"la=
tex">, note that:</p>
<ul>
<img src=3D"https://s0.wp.com/latex.php?latex=3D%5Cdisplaystyle+%5Cbegin%7B=
aligned%7D+a_1+%5Ccdot+x_0%26%5Cequiv+a_1+%5Ccdot+%28c_1+%5Ccdot+n_1+%5Ccdo=
t+w_1%2Bc_2+%5Ccdot+n_2+%5Ccdot+w_2%2B%5Ccdots%2Bc_t+%5Ccdot+n_t+%5Ccdot+w_=
t%29+%5C%5C%26%5Cequiv+a_1+%5Ccdot+c_1+%5Ccdot+n_1+%5Ccdot+w_1%2Ba_1+%5Ccdo=
t+c_2+%5Ccdot+n_2+%5Ccdot+w_2%2B%5Ccdots%2Ba_1+%5Ccdot+c_t+%5Ccdot+n_t+%5Cc=
dot+w_t++%5C%5C%26%5Cequiv+a_1+%5Ccdot+c_1+%5Ccdot+n_1+%5Ccdot+w_1+%5C%5C%2=
6%5Cequiv+a_1+%5Ccdot+c_1+%5C%5C%26%5Cequiv+b_1+%5C+%28%5Ctext%7Bmod%7D+%5C=
+m_1%29+%5Cend%7Baligned%7D&amp;bg=3Dffffff&amp;fg=3D333333&amp;s=3D0&amp;c=
=3D20201002" alt=3D"\displaystyle \begin{aligned} a_1 \cdot x_0&amp;\equiv =
a_1 \cdot (c_1 \cdot n_1 \cdot w_1+c_2 \cdot n_2 \cdot w_2+\cdots+c_t \cdot=
 n_t \cdot w_t) \\&amp;\equiv a_1 \cdot c_1 \cdot n_1 \cdot w_1+a_1 \cdot c=
_2 \cdot n_2 \cdot w_2+\cdots+a_1 \cdot c_t \cdot n_t \cdot w_t  \\&amp;\eq=
uiv a_1 \cdot c_1 \cdot n_1 \cdot w_1 \\&amp;\equiv a_1 \cdot c_1 \\&amp;\e=
quiv b_1 \ (\text{mod} \ m_1) \end{aligned}" class=3D"latex"><p></p>
</ul>
<p>In the above derivation, all the terms containing <img src=3D"https://s0=
.wp.com/latex.php?latex=3Dn_j&amp;bg=3Dffffff&amp;fg=3D333333&amp;s=3D0&amp=
;c=3D20201002" alt=3D"n_j" class=3D"latex"> with <img src=3D"https://s0.wp.=
com/latex.php?latex=3Dj+%5Cne+1&amp;bg=3Dffffff&amp;fg=3D333333&amp;s=3D0&a=
mp;c=3D20201002" alt=3D"j \ne 1" class=3D"latex"> drop out. This is because=
 <img src=3D"https://s0.wp.com/latex.php?latex=3Dn_j&amp;bg=3Dffffff&amp;fg=
=3D333333&amp;s=3D0&amp;c=3D20201002" alt=3D"n_j" class=3D"latex"> has <img=
 src=3D"https://s0.wp.com/latex.php?latex=3Dm_1&amp;bg=3Dffffff&amp;fg=3D33=
3333&amp;s=3D0&amp;c=3D20201002" alt=3D"m_1" class=3D"latex"> as a factor. =
The product <img src=3D"https://s0.wp.com/latex.php?latex=3Dn_1+%5Ccdot+w_1=
&amp;bg=3Dffffff&amp;fg=3D333333&amp;s=3D0&amp;c=3D20201002" alt=3D"n_1 \cd=
ot w_1" class=3D"latex"> drops out since <img src=3D"https://s0.wp.com/late=
x.php?latex=3Dw_1&amp;bg=3Dffffff&amp;fg=3D333333&amp;s=3D0&amp;c=3D2020100=
2" alt=3D"w_1" class=3D"latex"> is the multiplicative inverse if <img src=
=3D"https://s0.wp.com/latex.php?latex=3Dn_1&amp;bg=3Dffffff&amp;fg=3D333333=
&amp;s=3D0&amp;c=3D20201002" alt=3D"n_1" class=3D"latex"> modulo <img src=
=3D"https://s0.wp.com/latex.php?latex=3Dm_1&amp;bg=3Dffffff&amp;fg=3D333333=
&amp;s=3D0&amp;c=3D20201002" alt=3D"m_1" class=3D"latex">. Finally <img src=
=3D"https://s0.wp.com/latex.php?latex=3Da_1+%5Ccdot+c_1+%5Cequiv+b_1+%5C+%2=
8%5Ctext%7Bmod%7D+%5C+m_1%29&amp;bg=3Dffffff&amp;fg=3D333333&amp;s=3D0&amp;=
c=3D20201002" alt=3D"a_1 \cdot c_1 \equiv b_1 \ (\text{mod} \ m_1)" class=
=3D"latex"> since <img src=3D"https://s0.wp.com/latex.php?latex=3Dc_1&amp;b=
g=3Dffffff&amp;fg=3D333333&amp;s=3D0&amp;c=3D20201002" alt=3D"c_1" class=3D=
"latex"> is a solution of the equation <img src=3D"https://s0.wp.com/latex.=
php?latex=3Da_1+%5C+x+%5Cequiv+b_1+%5C+%28%5Ctext%7Bmod%7D+%5C+m_1%29&amp;b=
g=3Dffffff&amp;fg=3D333333&amp;s=3D0&amp;c=3D20201002" alt=3D"a_1 \ x \equi=
v b_1 \ (\text{mod} \ m_1)" class=3D"latex">. By the same reasoning, <img s=
rc=3D"https://s0.wp.com/latex.php?latex=3Dx_0&amp;bg=3Dffffff&amp;fg=3D3333=
33&amp;s=3D0&amp;c=3D20201002" alt=3D"x_0" class=3D"latex"> is the solution=
 to all the other equations in the system.</p>
<p>To see that the solution <img src=3D"https://s0.wp.com/latex.php?latex=
=3Dx_0&amp;bg=3Dffffff&amp;fg=3D333333&amp;s=3D0&amp;c=3D20201002" alt=3D"x=
_0" class=3D"latex"> is unique, see the proof in this previous post.</p>
